  "question": {
    "text": "Consider two identical galvanometers and two identical resistors with resistance R. If the internal resistance of the galvanometers <math><msub><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math> which of the following statement(s) about any one of the galvanometers<br />is(are) true ?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "hMoLq",
      "text": "The maximum voltage range is obtained when all the components are connected in series",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "7ctgl",
      "text": "The maximum voltage range is obtained when the two resistors and one galvanometer are connected in series, and the second galvanometer is connected in parallel to the first galvanometer",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "O44u9",
      "text": "The maximum current range is obtained when all the components are connected in parallel",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "D6PFo",
      "text": "The maximum current range is obtained when the two galvanometers are connected in series and the combination is connected in parallel with both the resistors.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/Phy_Papr2_12_Ans_1_.jpg\"/><br ><math><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math> <math><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><msub><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>E</mi><msub><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>E</mi><msub><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math><br ><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/Phy_Papr2_12_Ans_2_.jpg\"/><br ><math><msub><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></math> <math><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>×</mo><msub><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></math><br ><math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>×</mo><msub><